Game data in js/weather-data.js
  Zone names, weather names and weather percentages are facts and text from the
  FINAL FANTASY XIV game client. They are used under the FINAL FANTASY XIV Materials Usage
  Policy (https://support.na.square-enix.com/rule.php?id=5382&tag=authc), which requires the
  notice above.
  Source: the CSV export of the game tables in xivapi/ffxiv-datamining,
  https://github.com/xivapi/ffxiv-datamining, commit 52a72b38aa2f967cab36867f34cd9bee9debb88b
  (patch 7.58). That repository publishes no license of its own; only the tables named
  in tools/lib/gamedata.mjs are read, and only the rows for supported zones and nodes are kept.
  Checked against XIVAPI (https://v2.xivapi.com), whose capture is in
  tests/fixtures/xivapi-weather.json.

Game data in js/gathering-data.js
  Item names, places, levels, spawn times and folklore tome names of timed gathering nodes, from
  the same xivapi/ffxiv-datamining commit (GatheringPoint, GatheringPointBase, GatheringItem,
  GatheringPointTransient, GatheringRarePopTimeTable, GatheringSubCategory, ExportedGatheringPoint,
  Map, Item and related tables), under the same Materials Usage Policy. Checked against XIVAPI
  (tests/fixtures/xivapi-gathering.json) and against the node tables on the FFXIV wiki,
  https://ffxiv.consolegameswiki.com, pages "Unspoiled Nodes" (revision 1490944) and
  "Folklore Nodes" (revision 1491386). tests/fixtures/wiki-gathering.json holds only the facts
  read from those revisions (item, zone, times, coordinates, level, stars, tome); no wiki text.

Test vectors in tests/fixtures/weather-vectors.json
  Computed with ffxivweather 1.0.14 (https://github.com/karashiiro/ffxivweather-py, MIT) and
  confirmed with eorzea-weather 3.2.0 (https://github.com/flowercartelet/eorzea-weather, MIT).
  No code from either project is included here.

Lodestone headlines (Latest news)
  Headline titles, dates and categories are read when the page runs from the official Lodestone
  feeds, https://na.finalfantasyxiv.com/lodestone/news/topics.xml and news.xml, and link back to
  the Lodestone. They are FINAL FANTASY XIV text (c) SQUARE ENIX. None is stored in this
  repository except trimmed copies of the two feeds (five entries each, titles, dates and links,
  no article text) in tests/fixtures/lodestone-topics.xml and lodestone-news.xml, for the tests.

Reset times in js/resets.js
  Times and wording stated by Square Enix on the Lodestone, read on 2026-11-16: the Cactpot guide
  (https://na.finalfantasyxiv.com/lodestone/playguide/contentsguide/goldsaucer/cactpot/) for the
  Mini Cactpot and each data center's Jumbo Cactpot drawing, the patch 7.5 notes for the weekly
  reset, and the housing guide for the 5-day entry and 4-day results periods of the lottery. The
  daily reset, Grand Company and leve times come from the FFXIV wiki's Daily and Weekly Checklist
  (community sources) and are marked unverified on the page. The housing lottery's current period
  was compared once with PaissaDB (https://github.com/zhudotexe/FFXIV_PaissaDB); nothing from it is
  stored here.

Game data in js/market-items.js and radmagelabs/api/_ffxiv-prices/allow.mjs
  Names, item levels, HQ flags and market board categories of the items that can be sold on the
  market board, and the names of the data centers and worlds, from the same xivapi/ffxiv-datamining
  commit (Item, ItemSearchCategory, World and WorldDCGroupType), under the same Materials Usage
  Policy. data/market-items.lock.json records every sheet's SHA-256.

Market board prices (Market & Crafting)
  Prices, listings, completed sales, upload times and tax rates come, when the page runs, from
  Universalis (https://universalis.app), which collects them from players' market board visits.
  radmagelabs.com asks Universalis for them; nothing from Universalis is stored in this repository
  except answers captured once on 2026-11-17 for the tests, in tests/fixtures/universalis/ (see its
  manifest.json), with no player, retainer or listing names or ids.

Icons
  The weather icons and the crystal mark are original to this project. No game images are used.
